IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er1-self-employed-earnings`

-- Tests of er1-self-employed-earnings (Employment Insurance Regulations, regs 11.1 to 13). Piece er1.
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the Regulations (../../registers/source-bundle/SOR-96-332.txt), beside the assertion,
-- before the rule was run. The argument order is the order of the rule's GIVEN lines. Every ratio and amount below is
-- invented to exercise the arithmetic; none is a published figure.

§ `Regulation 11.1(2) - the floor of 1.0 (src:201)`

-- arguments: the amount before the year's adjustment; the ratio referred to in paragraph 4(2)(b)
#ASSERT `reg 11.1(2) the ratio after the floor of 1.0` 6000 0.9 EQUALS 1        -- 6000 x 0.9 = 5400, under $6,000: the ratio is deemed to be 1.0
#ASSERT `reg 11.1(2) the ratio after the floor of 1.0` 7000 0.8 EQUALS 1        -- 7000 x 0.8 = 5600, under $6,000
#ASSERT `reg 11.1(2) the ratio after the floor of 1.0` 7000 0.9 EQUALS 0.9      -- 7000 x 0.9 = 6300, not under $6,000: the ratio stands
#ASSERT `reg 11.1(2) the ratio after the floor of 1.0` 6250 0.96 EQUALS 0.96    -- 6250 x 0.96 = 6000 exactly: not "less than $6,000"
#ASSERT `reg 11.1(2) the ratio after the floor of 1.0` 6000 0.999 EQUALS 1      -- 5994
#ASSERT `reg 11.1(2) the ratio after the floor of 1.0` 6000 1 EQUALS 1          -- a ratio of exactly 1.0 is not "less than 1.0"
#ASSERT `reg 11.1(2) the ratio after the floor of 1.0` 6000 1.05 EQUALS 1.05    -- a ratio above 1.0 is never changed

§ `Regulation 11.1(3) - rounded down to the nearest dollar (src:202)`

#ASSERT `reg 11.1(3) the adjusted amount rounded down to the nearest dollar` 6073.8 EQUALS 6073
#ASSERT `reg 11.1(3) the adjusted amount rounded down to the nearest dollar` 6000 EQUALS 6000
#ASSERT `reg 11.1(3) the adjusted amount rounded down to the nearest dollar` 6000.99 EQUALS 6000

§ `Regulation 11.1(1) - the annual adjustment on a compound basis (src:200)`

-- one year: arguments: the amount before the year's adjustment; the ratio
#ASSERT `reg 11.1(1) the adjusted amount for the year` 6000 1.0123 EQUALS 6073    -- 6073.8 rounded down
#ASSERT `reg 11.1(1) the adjusted amount for the year` 6073 1.0123 EQUALS 6147    -- 6147.6979 rounded down
#ASSERT `reg 11.1(1) the adjusted amount for the year` 6000 0.9 EQUALS 6000       -- the ratio is deemed to be 1.0
#ASSERT `reg 11.1(1) the adjusted amount for the year` 7000 0.9 EQUALS 6300       -- 6300 is not under $6,000
#ASSERT `reg 11.1(1) the adjusted amount for the year` 6250 0.96 EQUALS 6000      -- exactly $6,000
-- the years: arguments: the amount in subparagraph 152.07(1)(d)(i); the ratios for 2012, 2013, ... in order
#ASSERT `reg 11.1(1) the adjusted amount after the years` 6000 EMPTY EQUALS 6000                                  -- no adjustment yet
#ASSERT `reg 11.1(1) the adjusted amount after the years` 6000 (LIST 1.0123) EQUALS 6073
#ASSERT `reg 11.1(1) the adjusted amount after the years` 6000 (LIST 1.0123, 1.0123) EQUALS 6147                 -- compound: the second year starts from 6073 (fork F11: 6148 if the rounding were left to the end)
#ASSERT `reg 11.1(1) the adjusted amount after the years` 6000 (LIST 1.0123, 0.9) EQUALS 6073                    -- 6073 x 0.9 = 5465.7, so the second ratio counts as 1.0
#ASSERT `reg 11.1(1) the adjusted amount after the years` 6000 (LIST 0.9) EQUALS 6000
#ASSERT `reg 11.1(1) the adjusted amount after the years` 7000 (LIST 0.9) EQUALS 6300
#ASSERT `reg 11.1(1) the adjusted amount after the years` 6000 (LIST 1.1, 1.1) EQUALS 7260                       -- 6600, then 7260
#ASSERT `reg 11.1(1) the adjusted amount after the years` 6000 (LIST 1.1, 1.1, 0.9) EQUALS 6534                  -- 7260 x 0.9 = 6534, not under $6,000: the ratio stands

§ `Regulation 12 - repealed (src:203)`

#ASSERT `reg 12 repealed in this text` EQUALS "reg 12: [Repealed, SOR/2016-206, s. 1]"

§ `Regulation 13 - the average number of weeks (src:206-207)`

-- 13(1) arguments: the maximum number of weeks under section 8 of the Fishing Regulations or subsection 12(2) of the Act; the weeks of benefits paid to the claimant
#ASSERT `reg 13(1) the average number of weeks of regular benefits of a claimant` 45 20 EQUALS JUST 12.5       -- (45 - 20) / 2
#ASSERT `reg 13(1) the average number of weeks of regular benefits of a claimant` 50 0 EQUALS JUST 25
#ASSERT `reg 13(1) the average number of weeks of regular benefits of a claimant` 45 45 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `reg 13(1) the average number of weeks of regular benefits of a claimant` 45 46 EQUALS NOTHING          -- more weeks paid than the maximum: the text does not say
-- 13(2) arguments: the maximum number of weeks under subsection 152.14(1) of the Act; the weeks of benefits paid to the self-employed person
#ASSERT `reg 13(2) the average number of weeks of benefits of a self-employed person` 26 10 EQUALS JUST 8
#ASSERT `reg 13(2) the average number of weeks of benefits of a self-employed person` 26 26 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `reg 13(2) the average number of weeks of benefits of a self-employed person` 26 27 EQUALS NOTHING
